(chiming music)

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.210
- Whenever you email Canvas @ Yale,

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.360
it's usually the one of the two of us,

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.740
so we do have faces.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.730
This is what we look like.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.670
We're always smiling when
we hear the complaints,

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.350
so it's great.
(audience chuckling)

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.340
We're actually talking about

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.860
the upcoming external apps in Canvas,

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.450
and one of the things we
did want to talk about

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.540
is what exactly is an external app.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.270
So an external app is a
third-party application

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.369
that can be embedded and integrated

00:00:31.369 --> 00:00:33.830
within Canvas seamlessly.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.010
We actually heard about one, Piazza,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.650
is actually a third-party app,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:41.260
so a lot of the tools that
you use, the sign-up tool

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.530
and a couple the other ones
that we were listening to,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.880
are considered third-party apps.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.670
They actually are really
great for if you want to

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:53.670
have a something in your class
that Canvas doesn't quite do,

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.840
there's an app for that, so it's great.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.200
We also want to talk about the process

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.980
of requesting external apps.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.710
There's a lot of technology out there

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.900
that can help your teaching

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.180
and we know that it can be
almost overwhelming to look at

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.570
all the technology available to you.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.990
So there is an external app request form

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.030
that you can fill out saying, hey,

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.500
I heard about this technology.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.303
I think will be beneficial,
can we integrate it?

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.460
That is step one.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.810
And we do have deadlines, so fall,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.910
you would have to request the
external app by March 1st,

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:34.010
spring is October 1st, and
summer is December 1st.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.450
Once the request for the
external app is created,

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.830
we then at the Center for
Teaching and Learning,

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.563
we get a demo of the app.

00:01:43.716 --> 00:01:46.320
After the demo, we say, hey,
this is really great tool.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.473
I think it could benefit
a lot of people at Yale.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.250
It goes through a wonderful process

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:58.210
where it's the OGC Registrar, ITS vetting.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:01:59.610
This step in the process

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.020
can take between weeks and
months of the process time,

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.330
so that's why we have the
deadline so far in advance

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.860
because it has to be ensured
that we're protecting

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.250
the student data and
the student information,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.740
because that's very
important to us as whole,

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.740
and to us who use that technology.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.330
Once it goes through that lovely process,

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.070
it actually then gets the
approval for the integration,

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.470
and then it gets integrated.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:28.640
The Canvas team will then
integrate it into the courses.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.950
We then have a pilot,

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.220
which can run about one to two semesters

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.210
depending on the pilot.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:36.130
It could be one course, it
could be an entire department,

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.330
or it could be university-wide.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.680
And then we also have
a post-pilot analysis,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.090
so that's what worked, what didn't work,

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.711
was this tool successful?

00:02:45.711 --> 00:02:47.890
This is the, essentially,
the entire process:

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.170
the external apps.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.193
It's really fun.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.510
(audience laughing)

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.230
Especially that vetting part.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.330
So the non-integrated external app use,

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.140
so say, for example, you found a tool

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.850
that you want to use in your class,

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.680
but you don't really want to
incorporate it or integrate it

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.440
in Canvas, you just want
to try it out first.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.640
Well, with that in mind, we
do want to be very cognizant

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.510
of what student data is
going to be out there,

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.340
so we are going to be working,
you can come to us, and say,

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.570
hey, I want to use this
app, can you please

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.460
help me make sure that
my students information's

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:27.000
not gonna be sold by Facebook
or anything like that?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.560
So you can actually work with us to ensure

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.930
that the data is gonna be protected

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:35.573
and what student information
is gonna be passed,

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.230
so that's the fun part,

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.900
and you can always email Canvas@Yale.edu

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.410
for any questions about this.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.010
We have been learning a
lot about this process,

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.280
and a lot of tools that you guys

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.800
